  [
    {
      "question": "How do I route webhook events to the right customer in a multi-tenant app?",
      "answer": "Webhook payloads include an event `id`, an `event_type`, and a `data` object. When an account has more than one newsletter, the `data` object also includes a `newsletter` ID, along with event-specific resource IDs (such as a `subscriber` or `email` ID).\n\nIf your application serves many Buttondown customers through a single endpoint, read `data.newsletter` to route each event to the right customer. You can also use per-customer webhook URLs or signing keys as a belt-and-suspenders check.\n\n[API keys](/api-introduction) are scoped to a single newsletter, so re-fetching a resource after a webhook notification requires knowing which customer's key to use — `data.newsletter` tells you that."
    }
